// lib/earth4/species-catalogue.js
// EARTH 4 — THE SPAWN CATALOGUE (the world feed, first use).
//
// Real species only: a stratified sample of the Catalogue of Life
// 2025 accepted-species list (COL25, DOI 10.48580/dgr6n) as delivered
// in ~/workspace/your_files/species-characteristics/ — living species
// of Animalia, Plantae and Fungi, up to 8 per class, best-recorded
// first. Nothing here is invented: every name, class, order, family,
// environment and size comes from the datasets.
// SIZES (Nov 14, 2026 — ~/workspace/earth4/build-species-sizes.py):
// every one of the 2,408 species now carries a size. sizeSource
// 'listed' is a real measurement from the dataset's size string
// (first length; thousands commas handled — "2,000 cm" is 20 m).
// Where the dataset holds no length for the species, sizeM is the
// median size of listed relatives in the full COL25 dataset —
// genus first, then family, order, class, phylum, kingdom —
// labelled 'estimated-genus' / '-family' / '-order' / '-class' /
// '-phylum' / '-kingdom'. An estimate is never presented as listed:
// the creature card shows "~X m" for estimates and "X m" for listed.
// Where the environment is inferred from the water-body column (no
// water body recorded = not aquatic) it says envSource 'inferred'.
// Rebuild the selection deterministically with
// ~/workspace/earth4/build-catalogue.py; re-enrich sizes with
// ~/workspace/earth4/build-species-sizes.py.
//
// Fields: name (scientific), kingdom, class, order, family,
// env (terrestrial | freshwater | marine | amphibious — the spawn
// rule: terrestrial spawns on land, freshwater/marine in water,
// amphibious on either), realm (first recorded biogeographic realm,
// '' when the dataset lists none), sizeM (metres), diet, habitat
// ('' when not recorded).
